+# yaml-language-server: $schema=https://docs.timenet.ai/schemas/dataset-card-v1.schema.json
+# Dataset Card for the uci/hydraulic connector: the single source for this dataset's metadata.
+# The connector loads it via DatasetMetadata.from_yaml(); the builder compiles it plus the schema
+# derived from the data into manifest.json.
+#
+# Signals are archival raw: every sensor keeps the rate and the unit that the release states, with
+# no resampling. The release has no official partition. The connector generates one; see
+# README.md for the split counts and the class coverage of each partition.
+yaml_schema_version: 1
+dataset_id: uci/hydraulic
+dataset_version: 1.0.0
+name: Condition Monitoring of Hydraulic Systems
+description: >-
+  2,205 load cycles of 60 s from a hydraulic test rig, each with 17 sensor signals at their
+  native rates: six pressures and the motor power at 100 Hz, two volume flows at 10 Hz, and four
+  temperatures, a vibration, the efficiency factor and two virtual cooling values at 1 Hz. Each
+  cycle has one classification task for each of four components: cooler (3 grades), valve (4),
+  internal pump leakage (3) and hydraulic accumulator (4). A stable flag marks the cycles where
+  static conditions might not have been reached yet. Generated 80/10/10
+  train/validation/test partitions use ten StratifiedGroupKFold folds with scikit-learn 1.9.1
+  and seed 42, grouped by the four-grade condition and stratified by the accumulator grade. These
+  are TimeNet-generated partitions, not official source splits; achieved sizes are 1,877 / 164 /
+  164 cycles because conditions stay whole.
+license: CC-BY-4.0
+license_url: https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by/4.0/legalcode
+source_url: https://archive.ics.uci.edu/dataset/447/condition+monitoring+of+hydraulic+systems
+citation: >-
+  Helwig, N., Pignanelli, E., Schuetze, A. (2015). Condition Monitoring of a Complex Hydraulic
+  System Using Multivariate Statistics. In Proc. I2MTC-2015, IEEE International Instrumentation
+  and Measurement Technology Conference, Pisa, Italy. https://doi.org/10.1109/I2MTC.2015.7151267
+domains:
+  - industrial
+tags:
+  - condition-monitoring
+  - fault-diagnosis
+  - hydraulics
+  - multivariate
+  - multi-rate
+  - classification
+  - uci
